A||||2||88formula||I need help with finding axle seals||||1||
Z||000000||88formula||08-08-2000||09:28 PM||||Where do I get the axle seals that go into the rear wheel hubs for an 88 Formula? Are they the same axle seals that go into the transmission?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gold-86SE||08-08-2000||10:01 PM||||<BR>From what I have seen when I pulled the rear end apart, no they are not the same. <P>To me, you should or at least ought to be able to purchase them at your local auto parts store, but if all else fails, try the pontiac dealership.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||08-08-2000||11:50 PM||||Bad news. That seal Might be available but don't hold your breath. It's usually sold only with the hub unit. (This is true of most all cars that use a bolt on hub.) If you go to buy a hub and there is no seal then check other hubs to make sure it's missing or not.<P>I recently wne tot buy for my caravan and the first one off the shelf was a returned unit in which the seal was hijacked. (Caravan hubs come with both the seal and new bolts. Fiero ones only come with the seal.)||||reg||1
